# ---- Analytics database (omnischools-analytics-prod) ----
# Oversight reads ONLY this DB. Locally, a second Docker Postgres or a Supabase branch.
# The app should connect as a NON-OWNER, read-scoped role so RLS applies (see db/sql/policies.sql).
ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://omnischools:omnischools@localhost:55432/omnischools_analytics_dev"

# ---- Gated named-record read-back to OPERATIONAL Postgres (OVERSIGHT_ANALYTICS_SPEC §6) ----
# Separate, scoped, logged connection used ONLY by the compliance record surface. Leave blank
# until that surface is wired. Never point the whole app at operational data.
#
# MUST be a dedicated read-only role on the OPERATIONAL project with an explicit per-table SELECT
# allow-list (staff_profile, ref_role, role_assignment, facilities_snapshot,
# school_staff_oversight_consent — and nothing else, notably NOT staff_compensation), no write/DDL,
# and a statement_timeout. Full posture + the exact GRANTs: docs/PROVISIONING.md §4a.
#
# UNSET = FAIL CLOSED. With this blank, the individual drill-down surface must refuse (aggregates
# only). Never fall back to ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL for it.
OPERATIONAL_READBACK_URL=

# ---- Supabase (analytics project — GES staff auth, NOT the school-auth project) ----
# REQUIRED AT RUNTIME whenever AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=false. They are validated as OPTIONAL so `next build`
# still succeeds on a machine with no deploy secrets (the build imports every route module), and
# enforced on the request path instead: with them unset, `getOfficerSession()` returns null, every
# gated surface refuses, and /sign-in renders an explicit "sign-in unavailable" state naming the
# missing variables. A BLANK value counts as unset — it does not crash the app.
#
# This is the ANALYTICS project's own Supabase Auth (the GES-staff pool), NOT omnischools-prod's: a
# head teacher and a GES district director are different identities in different projects.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ⚠ SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and must not be added.
# It bypasses RLS and every auth check in the project. Oversight's entire authorisation model is
# "the database decides" — the jurisdiction GUCs, the RLS policies, and the officer directory — so a
# runtime holding that key holds a credential able to read every named record in Ghana and to mint
# any officer, with no audit trail that could be trusted afterwards. The runtime does not read it
# (lib/env.ts has no entry for it) and tests/auth-boundaries.test.ts fails if any source file
# mentions it. The only privileged credential this app has is PROVISIONER_DATABASE_URL below, which
# is a narrow Postgres role rather than a project-wide master key.

# ---- Officer provisioning (increment G · Omnischools-operated admin console) ----
# The dedicated NON-OWNER provisioner role on the analytics project (docs/PROVISIONING.md §4b). It
# holds SELECT+INSERT on audit_officer_provisioning and SELECT+INSERT+UPDATE on
# ref_oversight_officer — never DELETE, and nothing else. It is the ONLY credential that can write
# authority, which is why it is separate from ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL (the app role has no write
# grant on either table, so self-promotion is a missing privilege rather than a policy decision).
#
# UNSET = FAIL CLOSED: the admin console refuses and `pnpm db:load-officers` exits. There is NO
# fallback to ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL and it must NEVER be the database owner.
PROVISIONER_DATABASE_URL=

# Comma-separated Supabase auth uids of the OMNISCHOOLS staff who may use the provisioning console.
# UNSET = nobody may provision (no bootstrap backdoor — adding the first administrator is a
# deploy-time act with a reviewer). A GES officer session is refused here at EVERY tier, including
# national: the most senior reader of the data must not also decide who may read it.
OVERSIGHT_ADMIN_UIDS=

# HMAC secret (>= 32 chars) for the two-person approval codes a REGION/NATIONAL grant requires.
# UNSET = no code can be minted or verified, so region/national provisioning refuses.
PROVISIONING_APPROVAL_SECRET=

# ---- Session policy (Kofi R5 / Lucy R3 — owner + DPO ratify these numbers) ----
# Absolute max-age is measured from the EARLIEST `amr` timestamp in the access token, never `iat`
# (which is rewritten on every hourly refresh, so an iat-based cap would silently never fire).
# An unmeasurable session age fails CLOSED. MFA is mandatory every session and has no escape hatch:
# recovery is the provisioning desk, not a self-service reset.
OVERSIGHT_SESSION_MAX_HOURS=8
OVERSIGHT_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES=30
# The §6 step-up reuse window: one fresh authenticator assertion covers browse → pick → view →
# export. Independent of the two timers above — a session well inside its 8h life still needs a
# fresh step-up once this lapses.
OVERSIGHT_STEP_UP_WINDOW_MINUTES=5

# ---- Public site URL (metadata; oversight.omnischools.gh in prod) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3100

# ---- Observability (dormant unless set) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# ---- Dev auth shim ----
# true = NATIONAL dev session (local dev). false + Supabase env = real GES-staff auth. FAIL CLOSED.
#
# PRECEDENCE: if this is true AND the Supabase vars are set, THE BYPASS WINS — and only outside
# production, where it cannot be reached at all (see below). One flag, one answer: the alternative
# ("real auth wins when its vars happen to be set") makes local behaviour depend on whether a
# developer's .env.local still holds a stale Supabase pair.
#
# ⚠ The shim returns a NATIONAL officer — the tier with NO jurisdiction filter — without
# authenticating anyone. In production that is unauthenticated national access to every named
# record, logged against a fabricated officer id. So the app REFUSES TO START when this is true and
# NODE_ENV=production (lib/auth/index.ts): a misconfigured deploy fails loudly at boot instead of
# quietly opening the door. Keep it true locally; it must be false on every deployed environment.
AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=true

# ---- E3 feature flag: individual drill-down of non-GES staff at NON-PUBLIC schools ----
# DEFAULT false, and it MUST stay false in production until a DPO writes the lawful-basis position
# for private/mission-school staff under the Data Protection Act 2012 (Act 843) — an employer's
# click is not the employee's consent (apps/web/Todo.md "Blocked on").
#
# false = a school whose ownership_type is PRIVATE or MISSION is refused the OTHER_STAFF individual
#         drill-down BEFORE any operational fetch, even if that school has recorded DPO consent.
#         The refusal is a logged DENIED_NO_CONSENT audit row, not a silent no-op.
# GES-establishment teachers are STATUTORY at every ownership type and never consult this flag.
E3_NON_PUBLIC_STAFF_DRILLDOWN=false
